ok></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKITA NOZOMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA SHINICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AICHIDENSHI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYOSHI, KENGO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKITA, NOZOMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, SHINICHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYOSHI KENGO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKITA NOZOMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA SHINICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYOSHI, KENGO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKITA, NOZOMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, SHINICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A data transmission method for eliminating ingress noise of a LAN using a CATV system.  A data transmission device (60) having an upper-layer cable modem (61) and a lower-layer cable modem (62) both connected in series is installed at the entrance of a network (50) in an apartment house. An upstream high-frequency modulated signal is converted to an Ethernet baseband signal by the lower-layer cable modem (62), which is modulated again by the upper-layer cable modem (61) and sent out.  Since ingress noise is analog signals, it is eliminated by the conversion.  Hence the data transmission quality is improved, a LAN cab be built even though the network is a network (50) in an apartment house involving much ingress noise.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de transmission de données permettant de supprimer l'entrée de bruit pour un réseau local qui utilise un système de télévision à antenne collective. Un dispositif de transmission de données (60), équipé d'un modem câble de couche supérieure (61) et d'un modem câble de couche inférieure (62) reliés en série, est monté à l'entrée d'un réseau (50) dans une résidence. Les signaux HF modulés en amont sont convertis en signaux de bande de base Ethernet par le modem câble de couche inférieure (62), lesquels sont de nouveau modulés par le modem câble de couche supérieure (61) et transmis. Etant donné que l'entrée de bruit se présente sous la forme de signaux analogiques, on la supprime par le biais de la conversion. Il en résulte une amélioration de la qualité de transmission des données et la possibilité d'établir un réseau local même si le réseau considéré est un réseau (50) de résidence qui fait intervenir une entrée de bruit importante.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>